{"skill":{"slug":"ai-meeting-notes","displayName":"AI Meeting Notes w/ Action Items + To-Do List Tracker"},"version":{"version":"1.0.3","createdAt":1770073179033,"changelog":"Version 1.0.3\n\n- Major update to clarify and enforce the meeting extraction response format.\n- Added a \"CRITICAL: RESPONSE FORMAT\" section detailing that all meeting results, action items, filename, and add-to-to-do-list prompt must be presented in ONE single message.\n- Made numbered action items in chat and to-do prompt mandatory for all outputs.\n- Strict naming and file attachment requirements enforced (e.g., filenames must be date-first).\n- Listed explicit rules for what to always/never do to ensure clarity and reliability for users.","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"assets/PREFERENCES-template.md","size":1629,"sha256":"1d4bfcaa29f966b741abeb3c1fe36601ec81faabca3fa6d7d49c86198c3e0ee5","contentType":null},{"path":"assets/TODO-template.md","size":1089,"sha256":"b4af7b6edfab92a8171b727dec99b5718a5870cef8e55aa7d3633b51beeb23ae","contentType":null},{"path":"examples/input-messy-notes.md","size":1010,"sha256":"72ef0edb9b014dcf9192ef20233de2dd3893ea2fcccad1df7b63d271d8a9d97d","contentType":null},{"path":"examples/input-transcript.md","size":2667,"sha256":"21a22eebd350b283ddc8cad7ec45f0b45c5b387fccb0627550ba08d49628e881","contentType":null},{"path":"examples/output-example.md","size":8550,"sha256":"f70517e1b997ee6c0953408522b46b3747f78ca15dbacb7838e2c18bea5dc374","contentType":null},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":25302,"sha256":"21aca0db7f5e75d78951f6edb3c43f3d8366e72d4cf6d666ad3db1f419f79b9a","contentType":null},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2376,"sha256":"0ac174c9540bb67989064ffdeedf0ef5564e5f799bf610bb15dec15702637472","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789029758793,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"a4d10148ce064feacbe6cd7c64037ec31fb57176ad94ddd85ef48d17f7f3f14d","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/a4d10148ce064feacbe6cd7c64037ec31fb57176ad94ddd85ef48d17f7f3f14d","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: ai-meeting-notes\nVersion: 1.0.3\n\nThe skill is designed to process meeting notes, extract action items, and manage a local to-do list. It instructs the AI to create and write to markdown files within a `meeting-notes/` directory and manage a `todo.md` file in the workspace. While these involve file system access and strong prompt instructions to the AI (in `SKILL.md` and `<ai_instructions>`), all actions are transparently aligned with the stated purpose of local note and task management. There is no evidence of data exfiltration, malicious execution, persistence mechanisms, or prompt injection aiming to subvert the agent for harmful objectives beyond the skill's advertised functionality.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779160973662},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":13,"checkedAt":1789029758793},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This meeting-notes skill is useful and mostly purpose-aligned, but it stores complete raw meeting content by default while also claiming nothing is stored.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Creating meeting-notes/ files and todo.md is aligned with the product, but plaintext raw transcripts, predictable filenames, and search across saved notes increase exposure in shared, synced, backed-up, or indexed workspaces.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"No install script, executable payload, dependency installation, remote retrieval, tool wrapping, or privilege-escalation mechanism was found in the inspected artifacts.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The instructions repeatedly require automatic saving, full markdown file attachment, raw-note preservation, and cross-meeting search. A display-only mode exists only when the user explicitly asks not to save, while the default behavior persists data.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The skill creates persistent local records containing metadata, attendees, action items, decisions, and raw pasted input. This conflicts with the FAQ statement that nothing is stored, creating a material informed-consent issue.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The core purpose is coherent: convert pasted notes or transcripts into summaries, action items, saved meeting files, searchable history, and a todo list. The concern is that complete raw notes are preserved and reattached by default, which can retain sensitive business or personal content beyond what users may expect.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Review before installing if you handle confidential meetings, customer data, HR/legal topics, financial details, or credentials in notes. Use it only in workspaces you trust, explicitly ask for no-save or summary-only handling when needed, and manually redact sensitive raw transcript content before sharing saved files or Slack-ready summaries.","findings":"[T09] unexpected: The static finding is supported in part: the artifact directs automatic plaintext retention of raw meeting content and includes a contradictory privacy statement. No executable payload, credential access, or external exfiltration was found.\n[SSD-3] expected: Saving meeting notes is part of the advertised workflow, but preserving the original input exactly and attaching the full file by default broadens redisclosure risk for sensitive transcripts.\n[SQP-2] unexpected: The artifact discloses auto-save in some places, but it does not provide a clear consent gate or prominent sensitivity warning before retaining full raw notes.\n[SDI-1] unexpected: The FAQ claim that nothing is stored conflicts with the automatic-save and raw-note retention instructions.\n[SDI-4] unexpected: The privacy-language contradiction is material because users may paste confidential meeting content believing it remains only in the conversation.\n[SQP-1] expected: Generic todo phrases such as showing todos or asking what is overdue are ordinary for a todo tracker; they are minor activation-scope concerns, not evidence of malicious behavior.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789029758793}}}}}